vlc: raise filter-chain MAX_CHAIN_LEVEL from 3 to 5

The filter chain solver in VLC's filter_chain.c bails out with
"Too high level of recursion (3)" when constructing chains that need
more than 3 filters in series. This occurs in practice when a user
combines two pixel-reading filters (e.g. postproc + autoupscale) with
hardware decode, because VLC must thread a hw->sw download converter
between the decoder and the first filter, pushing the chain to 4 deep:

    HW_decoder -> hw->sw_converter -> postproc -> autoupscale -> vout
                                          (already 3 levels into recursion)

Bumping MAX_CHAIN_LEVEL to 5 lets these chains construct without any
filter or syntax changes from the user's side. Higher values risk longer
chain-search times in pathological cases but the search is bounded by
the available filter modules; 5 is conservative.

Apply with:

    cd /path/to/vlc-source
    patch -p1 < /path/to/this/file.patch

Then rebuild VLC normally.

This patch is unaffiliated with VideoLAN; it's offered as a workaround
for a specific deep-chain scenario, not a recommended upstream change.
If you find it useful, consider sending it upstream with a clear
reproducer.

---

diff --git a/src/misc/filter_chain.c b/src/misc/filter_chain.c
--- a/src/misc/filter_chain.c
+++ b/src/misc/filter_chain.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
  * Local prototypes
  *****************************************************************************/

-#define MAX_CHAIN_LEVEL 3
+#define MAX_CHAIN_LEVEL 5

 /*****************************************************************************
  * Filter chain functions
